    "result_text": "All tests pass (BUILD SUCCESS). The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the GOLD membership tier rule: an owner's `membershipTier` becomes `GOLD` when their household (owners sharing the same `householdId`) has 3 or more members after their create; otherwise the existing SILVER/BRONZE rules apply.\n\nFollowing the codebase's established pattern (a point-in-time snapshot stored on the owner at create, like `namesakeCount`, then read by the mapper), the work is spread across small single-responsibility units:\n\n- **`AssignHouseholdSize`** (new function step) \u2014 records the household size after this create: existing members sharing the `householdId` plus the new owner (`+1`). Wired into `owners.POST.yml` right after `AssignHousehold` (so the id is assigned/back-filled) and before `SaveOwner`.\n- **`Households.memberCount(...)`** (new helper) \u2014 counts existing owners carrying a given `householdId`, reusing the shared household grouping utility rather than duplicating iteration logic.\n- **`Owner`** \u2014 added the persisted `householdSize` field/column (`household_size`) added to all four schema DDLs (hsqldb, h2, postgres, mysql).\n- **`OwnerMapper.membershipTier`** \u2014 returns GOLD when the stored `householdSize >= 3`, else falls through to the unchanged SILVER/BRONZE logic.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `GOLD` to the `membershipTier` enum (the `OwnerDto` is generated from this) and updated its description.\n\nFor a shared household of three, the members are stamped with sizes 1, 2, 3 as they're created \u2014 so the third resolves to GOLD, matching the acceptance test. The full test suite is green.",
